                        "glosses": [
                            "External; outward; not inherent"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "obsolete",
                            "rare"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f722e73c-ea8a-4ec5-b78b-49bed163cb36",
                                "sense_id": "dab34340-d6ca-3cc3-ad75-4a885f37e9c4",
                                "text": "Heaven is my judge, not I for love and duty, / But seeming so, for my particular end, / For when my outward action doth demonstrate / The native act and figure of my heart / In complement extern, 'tis not long after / But I will wear my heart upon my sleeve / For daws to peck at."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f428beb7-b7da-4818-b7a5-61b39d501ef0",
                                "sense_id": "dab34340-d6ca-3cc3-ad75-4a885f37e9c4",
                                "text": "For if the ſoul of man vvere emancipated by virtue, it vvould not need any regulation or monition, beſides that of its invvard Tribunal; vvhich becauſe ſin does uſurp upon, has ſome relief from thoſe extern adjuments."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
