                                "example_id": "aad8e07b-4538-4a33-a339-2da1152b9875",
                                "sense_id": "3be8ecd5-6cc3-3707-844b-140499d7b4b0",
                                "text": "Finally, get rid of the two function declarations and two externs that we added at the top of TEFIL.CPP so that we could support file_open()."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "309151bc-1b84-4343-a657-d59fa1e4a46b",
                                "sense_id": "3be8ecd5-6cc3-3707-844b-140499d7b4b0",
                                "text": "This is probably the big thing with C++, the more you can avoid global concepts and nasty externs the better, an object/class should be totally self-contained."
